    The bug: `Heritage` built the property triple for the ops it creates from a
    hand-written local table that gave CPUI_MULTIEQUAL only the `marker` flag,
    where upstream's `TypeOpMulti` (typeop.cc:1946) carries
    `special|marker|nocollapse`.  `getEvalType()` therefore answered 0 instead
    of `special`, so `ScopeLocal::annotateRawStackPtr` (varmap.cc:396) did not
    recognise the phi that reads the raw input stack pointer as a special op and
    spliced its zero-offset `PTRSUB(sp,#0)` placeholder in FRONT of it, inside
    the block's leading phi run.  `ConditionalJoin::cutDownMultiequals`
    (blockaction.cc:1981) then stopped at that PTRSUB while removing one in-edge
    slot from each phi of the joined exit block, leaving the phis behind it with
    one input more than their block has in-edges; the next read of a phi slot
    against the parent's in-edge vector is out of bounds.

    Single pass, default pipeline.  Pre-fix `print C` renders the error stub
    `void scan_list(void)` carrying the LOSS-131 warning and nothing else, so
    all five assertions fail; post-fix the loop, both calls and the parameters
    come back and all five pass.
